Relevant columns and their roles  

• Belts.id – primary‑key of the title table; lets us know which “belt” (title) was on the line in a match.  
• Belts.name – text name of the title; we will look for titles that contain the word “NXT”.  
• Matches.title_id – foreign‑key to Belts.id; tells us which title was defended in each match.  
• Matches.duration – text run‑time of the match; we will order by this to find the shortest one.  
• Matches.title_change – 1 = new champion, 0 = no change; we must exclude all rows where this is 1.  
• Matches.winner_id – id of one wrestler in the match (links to Wrestlers.id).  
• Matches.loser_id – id of the other wrestler in the match (links to Wrestlers.id).  
• Wrestlers.id – primary‑key of the wrestler table.  
• Wrestlers.name – the wrestler’s ring name; we will ultimately return these two values.  

Main conditions we will eventually need  
1.  Belts.name   LIKE '%NXT%'            -- select only NXT titles  
2.  Matches.title_change = 0             -- ignore matches with a title change  
3.  Matches.duration IS NOT NULL         -- avoid missing times  
4.  After filtering, pick the MIN(duration) (or ORDER BY converted seconds LIMIT 1).  

──────────────────────  
Ten exploratory → final SQL statements
(Each query LIMITs the output to 20 rows and is annotated.)

```sql
-- 1. List every belt that contains the word “NXT”.
SELECT DISTINCT b.id, b.name
FROM Belts AS b
WHERE b.name LIKE '%NXT%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Show all matches that involve an NXT belt (any result).
SELECT m.id,
       m.title_id,
       m.duration,
       m.title_change
FROM Matches AS m
JOIN Belts   AS b ON b.id = m.title_id
WHERE b.name LIKE '%NXT%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Same as #2 but be sure there was NO title change.
SELECT m.id,
       m.title_id,
       m.duration
FROM Matches AS m
JOIN Belts   AS b ON b.id = m.title_id
WHERE b.name LIKE '%NXT%'
  AND m.title_change = 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Add both wrestler id columns to see who was involved.
SELECT m.id,
       m.winner_id,
       m.loser_id,
       m.duration
FROM Matches AS m
JOIN Belts   AS b ON b.id = m.title_id
WHERE b.name LIKE '%NXT%'
  AND m.title_change = 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Order those non‑title‑change matches by duration
--    (lexicographical, quick glance) to eyeball the top few.
SELECT m.id,
       m.duration
FROM Matches AS m
JOIN Belts AS b ON b.id = m.title_id
WHERE b.name LIKE '%NXT%'
  AND m.title_change = 0
  AND m.duration <> ''
ORDER BY m.duration          -- quick first pass
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Convert the MM:SS duration into total seconds
--    (works when the format is 'MM:SS' or 'HH:MM:SS').
--    Here we show the 20 shortest.
SELECT m.id,
       m.duration,
       (CAST(substr(m.duration,1,instr(m.duration,':')-1) AS INTEGER) * 60 +
        CAST(substr(m.duration,instr(m.duration,':')+1)        AS INTEGER)
       ) AS seconds_total
FROM Matches AS m
JOIN Belts AS b ON b.id = m.title_id
WHERE b.name LIKE '%NXT%'
  AND m.title_change = 0
  AND m.duration LIKE '%:%'
ORDER BY seconds_total
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Grab the single shortest NXT title match (no title change) by id.
SELECT m.id
FROM Matches AS m
JOIN Belts AS b ON b.id = m.title_id
WHERE b.name LIKE '%NXT%'
  AND m.title_change = 0
  AND m.duration LIKE '%:%'
ORDER BY
  (CAST(substr(m.duration,1,instr(m.duration,':')-1) AS INTEGER) * 60 +
   CAST(substr(m.duration,instr(m.duration,':')+1)        AS INTEGER)
  )
LIMIT 1;
```

```sql
-- 8. Now pull the wrestler‑ids from that single match id (replace ? with id from #7).
SELECT m.winner_id,
       m.loser_id
FROM Matches AS m
WHERE m.id = ?              -- <- supply id from query #7
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Convert those wrestler‑ids into names.
SELECT w.name
FROM Wrestlers AS w
WHERE w.id IN (?, ?)        -- <- winner_id and loser_id from #8
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final single‑shot query: shortest NXT title match (no title change) with both names.
SELECT wr1.name AS wrestler_1,
       wr2.name AS wrestler_2
FROM Matches   AS m
JOIN Belts     AS b   ON b.id   = m.title_id
JOIN Wrestlers AS wr1 ON wr1.id = m.winner_id
JOIN Wrestlers AS wr2 ON wr2.id = m.loser_id
WHERE b.name LIKE '%NXT%'
  AND m.title_change = 0
  AND m.duration LIKE '%:%'
ORDER BY
  (CAST(substr(m.duration,1,instr(m.duration,':')-1) AS INTEGER) * 60 +
   CAST(substr(m.duration,instr(m.duration,':')+1)        AS INTEGER)
  )
LIMIT 1;
```

